{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>and they became a sign</b> — their assembly became a sign and a remembrance." "<b>לנס</b> — three times in the Masorah: כמסרה, ויהיו לנס, שורש ישי אשר עומד לנס עמים, שש ברקמה וגו'. היה מפרשך להיות לך לנס — this is what is meant: a place was fenced off for them; when the earth opened, a place remained in the middle, like the נס (banner) that is at the top of the mast. So too a mast-place remained. And from here is a hint for those who say that they are a lost item sought after, to stand at the resurrection of the dead in the days of the Messiah — and that is שורש ישי אשר עומד לנס עמים."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The three Masorah citations are identified as: Numbers 26:10, Isaiah 11:10, and possibly Numbers 15:38 (תכלת בגדילות, related to שש ברקמה). The phrase היה מפרשך is obscure and translated hyper-literally; possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:14.355673628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}